Greptile's rule about unreproduced behaviour claims caught a claim that was not merely unreproduced but WRONG. The launcher docstring said the auditor 'treats any file whose first two bytes are a shebang as executable shell'. Reproduced against the real auditor, that is false: a shebang says a file executes, not that it executes AS shell, and only a shebang naming a shell interpreter makes the body shell input.

Measured by writing this file into a throwaway git repository under four shebangs and calling verify():
  #!/bin/bash          -> the file is reported by name (scanned as shell)
  #!/usr/bin/env sh    -> reported by name
  #!/usr/bin/env node  -> NOT reported (not shell input)
  no shebang           -> NOT reported, which is why this file has none

The same wrong sentence is present in all seven repositories carrying this launcher, which is what propagating a fleet change by copying a reference file produces: the error travels with the text. Corrected here and in the five sibling convergence branches; pm-csv already has it on main and needs the same correction separately.

The claim is now reproduced in the suite rather than asserted.
